TYPES.md §5.3, §7.2, DECISIONS 460: the operand of a negation is still a 64-bit Int, so `-(9223372036854775808)` is E3201 on its operand, with or without an expected type: into an Int, as a parameter default, as a field default and alone. `-(-9223372036854775808)` is E3201 on its value 9223372036854775808, with or without an expected type; `-(-(-9223372036854775808))` is reported once, at the negation that leaves the Int range. The operand is not what is stored, so its finding names no declaration; a negation's value names the declaration it is stored into only when the type the message names, Int, is that declaration's type (`twice`, not `q: Int8`), and one inside another negation names none (API.md §4.4 F12).
